## 5. In Case of Defect Found

| Step | Point Person | Expected Actions | Remarks |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **1. Defect found** | [Developer], [QA] | 1. Report the issue in the project team channel.<br>2. Acknowledge any report received from support or stakeholders. | [Fill in if a defect occurs] |
| **2. Information sharing** | [Product Owner / Business Analyst] | Inform the Product Owner via the stakeholder channel. If end users are directly affected, inform operations. | |
| **3. Investigation** | [Developer], [QA] | 1. Reproduce the issue in staging.<br>2. Investigate the codebase, logs and data.<br>3. Confirm impact and share with the team. | |
| **4. Reporting findings** | [Developer], [QA] | Share bug size, affected users/records, recommendation, and estimated fix time. | |
| **5. Decision** | [Product Owner / Project Manager] | Decide: **immediate rollback** or **hotfix** (see decision guide below). | |
| **6. End result** | Project Team | Announce the outcome in the project, stakeholder and operations channels. | |

**Decision guide (rollback vs. hotfix)**

| Condition | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Affects all users or a critical flow (e.g., users cannot log in, core transaction fails) | **Rollback** |
| Affects specific conditions only and a fix can be released **within a day** | **Hotfix** |
| Fix will take **more than a day** | **Rollback**, then re-release with the fix |
| Cosmetic / low impact (typos, labels, layout) | **Bug ticket / next scheduled patch** |
| A scheduled job is producing incorrect data | **Disable the job immediately**, then investigate and correct data |

