## 6. Contingency Plan

### 6.1 Risk Identification and Severity Rating

> List realistic failure scenarios **before** the release. Severity: Critical / Major / Minor / Trivial. Probability and Impact: Low / Medium / High.

| # | Scenario | Severity | Probability | Impact | Mitigation (before release) | Action Plan (if it happens) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Scheduled job did not run on time | Major | [ ] | [ ] | Tested in staging and UAT | - Check job logs and schedule configuration<br>- Trigger the job manually<br>- If it persists: hotfix the schedule or ask DevOps to run it manually |
| 2 | Scheduled job ran only partially (missing records in the summary report) | Major | [ ] | [ ] | Tested in staging and UAT | - Identify affected records from the summary email<br>- Check for data inconsistency with the dependent service<br>- Run data correction / submit data update request<br>- Re-run the job for specific records |
| 3 | Wrong business rule / threshold applied to users | Major | [ ] | High | Boundary-value testing, UAT | - Disable the job<br>- Check result records<br>- Submit data correction request<br>- Hotfix |
| 4 | Restriction / action applied to users who should be excluded | Critical | [ ] | High | User-type coverage testing | - Disable the job<br>- Lift the restriction via admin tool<br>- Correct history records<br>- Inform operations of affected users |
| 5 | Bulk file upload / import fails | Major | [ ] | Medium | Tested valid and invalid files | - Hotfix or rollback of that component only<br>- Prepare a component-specific rollback branch in advance |
| 6 | Configuration / reference data missing in production | Major | Low | Medium | Data request reviewed | - Re-run table creation / initial data request<br>- Verify API endpoints |
| 7 | API authentication / integration failure between services | Major | Low | Medium | Code review, staging testing | - Hotfix; use manual workaround in admin tool meanwhile |
| 8 | User-facing core feature unusable (e.g., cannot enter live session, cannot complete transaction) | Critical | Low | High | Staging and UAT | - Investigate<br>- Hotfix if limited to specific conditions<br>- Rollback if all users are affected |
| 9 | Email notification not sent / wrong template sent | Minor–Major | Low | Medium | Template verification in staging | - Hotfix or patch<br>- Resend / compensate affected users if needed |
| 10 | Input validation accepts invalid values (empty, decimal, special characters) | Minor | Low | Low | Negative testing | - Bug fix in next patch |
| 11 | UI state issue (e.g., button always enabled) | Minor | Low | Low | UI testing | - Bug fix in next patch |
| 12 | Spelling, label or paragraph order errors | Trivial | Low | Low | Copy review | - Bug fix in next patch |

